{
 "_comment": "Recorded-shape GitHub REST fixture for loom-daemon ci_telemetry tests (#8824): a synthetic org with 2 active repos x 3 completed runs x 4 jobs, plus one archived repo that must never be polled. Keys are request paths with the `created` watermark query parameter removed; `next` mirrors the Link rel=next header. Run k of each repo lasts k*60s; job j lasts j*10s. Job logs (#8825) live under `job_logs`, keyed by the same request path shape: `text` is served verbatim (BOM included, exactly as GitHub's text/plain job-log response arrives), `repeat` builds a large log without committing megabytes, and `status` forces a failure. A job with no entry gets a one-line synthesized log. Neither credential-shaped string below is real: they exist to prove the daemon forwards what GitHub sent, because the gateway is the redaction boundary. Beta's three runs carry a `head_commit` (#9337 trigger attribution: an ordinary subject, the #8508 re-date subject, and a merge-from-main subject); alpha's deliberately do not, proving an absent `head_commit` still deserializes. Two alpha jobs carry a `steps[]` array (#9089 step spans): 10012 (four steps, all with timestamps) and 10034 (a failing step followed by one the job never reached, which has neither timestamp and must therefore produce no span); every other job has no `steps[]` at all, proving a pre-#9089 recording still deserializes. Alpha run 1001 additionally has an artifacts listing (#9089 suite spans) naming one `ci-suite-timings-2` record, one unrelated artifact that must never be downloaded, and one expired timings artifact that must be skipped; the downloadable artifact bodies live under `artifacts`, keyed by artifact name. Run 1001's job 10014 is a `nextest-partition` leg (`Rust Unit Tests (2/3)`) and the same listing names its `ci-test-timings-rust-unit-tests-2-3` JUnit upload (#9456 per-test spans), whose body is real nextest JUnit shape: a self-closing pass, a `<failure>` whose escaped text embeds a decoy `<testcase>` the parser must not read, a `<flakyFailure>`, a sub-floor test, a `<skipped/>`, one with no `timestamp`, one whose clock is skewed outside the job window, a repeat of an earlier (classname, name), and the same test name under a second binary.",
